"Chatelard" <piper.lyon@wanadoo.fr> writes:

> Hi,
> 
> I want to add one processor on an Alpha server 2100 running Tru64 UNIX
> Version 4.0F .
> Does anyone knows where i can find documentation to do this.

No, but I've shuffled CPUs between 2100 systems. Basically you unscrew
the left side of the frame; the screws are at the front, the left
sheet will swing out on hinges. Then you clean out the dust...

The cpus are in horizontal slots toward the back; the memory boards
are in there, too. Just plug in the cpu; I don't remember if there
were any screws to fasten. There probably were.  My systems had some
plastic sheets in them to guide airflow across the heat sinks.

Touch grounded metal first. Wear a wrist strap if you like. Take off
rubber-soled shoes. Don't comb your hair. Perform any other
static-preventing activity before touching the boards.

Then close the casing again.

Rebuild the kernel, if you like (can't remember if this was necessary;
hardware changes often necessitate it, though): If you can't boot the
old kernel, use the generic kernel (">>> boot -fi genvmunix"). Then
run doconfig to build the kernel. Don't forget to move the new kernel
to /vmunix. Reboot.

I can't think of any other advice. I'm sure to have left out the
important bits, of course.

Florian

