Once upon a time, Mitsura <mitsura@village.uunet.be.anitspam> said:
>does anybody have a working OpenSSH client on Tru64 v5.1
>I have tried to compile it, but it does not seem to compile.

That's a pretty vague error report.

I'm using OpenSSH 2.9.9p2, compiled with Compaq's C compiler, just fine
on 4.0F and 5.1A.

You need to have OpenSSL and zlib installed to build OpenSSH and then
need PRNGD installed to run it.  With that, you can configure like:

CC="cc -std1" CFLAGS="-O -I/usr/local/include" LDFLAGS="-L/usr/local/lib" \
./configure \
	--with-osfsia \
	--with-default-path=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/usr/bin/X11 \
	--with-prngd-socket=/var/run/egd-pool \

