andy thomas wrote:

> Running netsetup to add the IP alias 137.73.192.59 to a network interface
> tu0 already configured with the address 137.73.192.7 produces the
> following strange ipconfig invocation:

...

> Is netsetup broken (this is on a DU 4.0D system)? And what is the correct
> ifconfig incantation for doing this?

You should not configure both a primary and alias IP address with
the same ifconfig command, in future releases ifconfig was changed
to complain and do nothing.  IP aliases should be put into /etc/inet.local,
it's run at boot-time after the other addresses are added to the system.
The line would look something like this:

    ifconfig tu0 alias 137.73.192.59 netmask 255.255.255.0

-Brian

