Bob Ceculski wrote in message ...
>
>we will not move from alpha vms to itanic vms if the following is true
>...
>
>
>but the itanium can not replace the alpha at all:
>- what is with the hardware failure detection mechanism of the alpha
>cpu? a defective memory never crashes a machine - itanium will do so.
>


Excuse me?  What in the heck are you trying to say here?

The only "detectable" CPU "failure" that I know of is correctable bcache
errors, which indicate a failing bcache.  Any error that causes a CPU to not
work correctly, or to simply stop executing, are generally catestrophic on
Alpha - or on Itanium.  Even if the CPU failure doesn't take down or hang
the entire system, the entire system MUST be brought down, because you have
no way of knowing what damage the failed CPU may be doing (like corrupting
things).

Defective memory WILL crash a system if it is an uncorrectable memory error
on VAX, and on Alpha, and on Itanium.  The ONLY case where this is not true
is the VAX 9000, which has special VMS logic to try and run down the failed
address, and see if it can simply shoot a process, rather than crash.

Alpha systems with ECC memory survive single bit errors.  So will Itanium.
You can build a Alpha system or a Itanium system with Parity memory instead
of ECC - in which case the system will crash on a simgle bit error.  It is
pretty unlikely you will ever see this on any server from Compaq.

In fact, memory systems are being designed with Raid-5 technology to survive
multi-bit errors - somethig needed when you see max memory sizes reaching >
1TB.

>
>itanic vms better be as reliable as alpha vms or forget it ... we will
>not
>run on a blue screen platform like nt ...

It will be.

The main reasons for system unreliability do NOT involve the CPU chip.

IMHO, the leading causes of unreliability:

    1) System, driver and application SW
    2) Unreliable devices
    3) Cheap components

#1 is the software, which *can* include in the case of a "PC" the BIOS.
Itanium is NOT a BIOS based system.

I see absolutely NO reason to believe that Itanium based servers from Compaq
running OpenVMS will have any less quality or reliability than Alpha based
servers.






