In a previous article, Alan Greig <a.greig@virgin.net> wrote:

->Anyone with ES40s seen the LCD display "12V BULK WARN" appear on power
->up? The last time we powered down one of our ES40s it booted up with
->"12V BULK WARN" on the LCD display. We called FS and they replaced the
->power supply. We just had to power down this system for 24 hours again
->prior to electrical work and on power up the system is again
->displaying the same warning. The system is operating normally and I am
->about to call field service again but am wondering if anyone else has
->seen this and could the problem be with a sensor rather than the power
->supply itself? Anyone else seen this warning and what did FS do to fix
->it?

See table 7-2 (RMC error messages) in your owners manual. Also, to see
the value of the +12V supply, get into RMC (CTRL[CTRL[RMC at the
console) and type ENV at the RMC prompt. It gives you a nifty display
of all the environmental values and blinks those that are out of range.

We had a "CPU0 VCORE WARN" recently. Those voltages are regulated on the
"PCI board" (the PCI motherboard) which is a real dog to remove. I can't
imagine that the +12 is regulated any other place than the PS. I suppose
it could be the +12 sensor too (wherever that is).


