> What solution to things like the single registry namespace do you see?

A serious application can simply use its own configuration files instead of
relying on that stupid registry thing. Or they could improve the registry
thing to allow each process to have access to its own registry space. Instead
of having just "USER", it could have "JOB" and "PROCESS". This way, you could
start IIS on the same machine with the same "USER", but with a different
"PROCESS" registry section/tree with the process specific parameters.


