Hans Schwengeler wrote:
> 

> > I kept getting an error message saying "No space left on device".
> > What other command can I use so it works on both platform?
> > Thanks in advance
> > Paul

>         well, the same thing happens quite often here. In such a case you
> have to use GNU tar instead of the system supplied tar. GNU tar works ok,
> whereas the DEC tar has some known problems. (I use GNU tar (gtar) version
> 1.13, available at http://sunsite.cnlab-switch.ch for example).
> 

Solaris use 'variable block mode' for DATs and Exabytes by default,
where other Unices like SGI and AIX often use fixed tape blocks (like
with the old QIC tape drives, which used 512bytes/block). Make sure that
yu use the correct tape device, then try to provide the blocking factor
explicitely: start with tar tvbf 20 /dev/???, and then jump to 64 and
126 (which is often used on Suns). 'No space left on device' is a system
call level error, so tar has just openend the tape device and tried to
read the first block. If the blocksize is too small, this error might
happen.

