Try a simple bit of 'C' code:

    union {
        short s;
        char  c[2];
    } endian;

    endian.s = 1;
    if ( endian.c[0] == 1 )
        printf( "Little Endian\n" );
    else
        printf( "Big Endian\n" );

Also, I looked at some examples of BIG_ENDIAN and LITTLE_ENDIAN use,
and it seems the correct way to use it is to say:

    if ( BYTE_ORDER == LITTLE_ENDIAN )
        printf( "Little Endian\n" );
    else
        printf( "Big Endian\n" );

