>`s  ok, but when i reboot i lose this change and network is not configurate.
>What can i do to set these change permanent?
>thanks in advance.
>Cesar
>

Hi,

for 4.0x (as I only know) thats not a problem.
(for the example, the assumption is: your netrain Interface will be
the first interface of the node, there are two diual ethernet NICs
with ee0 - ee3 in the node, the physical interfaces for netrain are
ee0 and ee2, Adresses as shown below)
Edit the file /etc/rc.config with the following line

.....
NETDEV_0="nr0"
NETDEV_1="ee1"
.....
IFCONFIG_0="192.168.100.100 netmask 255.255.255.0 add ee0,ee2"
IFCONFIG_1="10.0.0.2 netmask 255.255.255.248"
....

That all. If you want to add some tuning for faster failover, do it
with then kernel parameters for netrain. The corresponding parameters
can not be set in rc.config diretly.

Good luck,

Axel


