Derek,

I tend to use the zeero utility.  (/usr/lbin/zeero)

This writes zeros to every block of the disk.  If I remember correctly, I do:

    /usr/lbin/zeero -d /dev/disk/dsk<n>c

I usually do this to eliminate any confusion from "old data" that was written
to the disk.

No, this isn't really a format, but it works for me.

-Derek Haining



