"Thierry" <thierry.constant2@wanadoo.fr> wrote in message news:3bc203ca$0$1566$626a54ce@news.free.fr...
> Hi,
>
> What is the right procedure to create a system backup on OSF1 4.X ?
>
> What the procedure to recover if I have a crash ?
I assume no LSM because I'm lazy...
Create copies of each disklabel on the root filesystem and on paper that you keep with backup media.
To back up, use vdump to copy each filesystem to tape[s].
To recover..
Boot from CD
Exit to shell
Relabel root disk (/ /usr /var etc)
Make filesystems for new partitions.
Mount / /usr and /var
Recover / /usr and /var from tape using vrecover.
Reboot from recovered system disk.
Recover data as needed either from the vdump set or from some other more recent set of backups.





