> I also have a process dubbed "-" when I use the w command showing up
> being run from a remote machine. Its been running for 38days and yet I
> can not find any reference to this process in ps(looking for it based on
> the console its running on).

Generally the only way to get rid of a defunct process is by rebooting.
It's generally a sign that its parent (which you can also get via `ps')
isn't doing something it should be (waiting on the child, or ignoring
SIGCLD/SIGCHLD).

The second problem you mention (something showing up with `w' that isn't there)
is probably a corruption of your utmp file.  It may be related to the
other problem you're having, but they technically are two separate issues.

Tim
