Gary Gale wrote:
> 
> Does anyone know whether you can invoke an external script from within
> a setld SCP during the C phase of a product installation?
> Specifically, if I've got a script file which is installed in between
> PRE_L and POST_L, can I invoke it during the configuration phase?
> 

I would guess you can.

Lots and lots of examples of .scp scripts can be found in the OS setld
inventory
directory, /usr/.smdb./ 
Many of these do funky things during the C phase, including invoking
external programs.
E.g., see COLBASE200.scp which calls rcmgr. Others I've taken a quick
peek at do mkdir's,
etc. The DIABASExxx.scp script seems to do a particularly gruesome set
of tasks.
There are even helpful looking comments in some of these about potential
problems with setld.

Remember also that setld is just a script itself...

